# Agent discipline (applies to every session)

You are executing ONE lane file from `plans/`. Rules:

1. **Read your assigned `plans/W*.md` file first, fully.** It is the contract.
2. **Touch only files in your lane's allowlist.** If a fix seems to require
   editing a file outside it, STOP and report — do not improvise.
3. **One commit per checklist item**, message: `W<lane>.T<item>: <summary>`.
4. **Run the acceptance command(s) before declaring an item done.** Paste the
   output (or describe the rendered artifact) in your report.
5. **Never refactor opportunistically.** Out-of-scope cleanups are forbidden
   even if they look easy.
6. **Schemas in `docs/contracts/` and `config/design_tokens.json` are frozen.**
   If your task seems to need a schema change, STOP and report.
7. All visual constants (colors, fonts, glow, timing, safe areas) come from
   `config/design_tokens.json` — never hardcode hex values or font names.
8. New assets (icons, fonts, SFX, models) enter only via `tools/prepare_assets.py`
   and `assets/manifest.json` — never download ad hoc. Every asset entry needs
   a license field.
9. If a checklist item is ambiguous, implement the narrowest reading and flag
   the ambiguity in your report rather than expanding scope.
10. Final report format: per item — what changed, how verified, open concerns.
